1
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:39,914
Just here, please.

2
00:00:39,998 --> 00:00:42,167
The Unitia Airlines passengers
will be arriving soon.

3
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:43,084
Okay!

4
00:00:43,168 --> 00:00:44,586
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

5
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:45,503
Hayami.

6
00:00:46,671 --> 00:00:47,547
Here.

7
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:50,049
What's this?

8
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:52,135
Draft manuals from the airport director.

9
00:00:52,218 --> 00:00:55,305
They say our booth has too many issues.
We need to standardize the procedures.

10
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:58,141
-They've totally got their eyes on us.
-Now, now.

11
00:00:58,224 --> 00:01:01,436
If you have any feedback, Hayami,
you're an expert with these documents.

12
00:01:01,519 --> 00:01:05,148
Right, after all, you were on the career
track at the Ministry of Justice.

13
00:01:05,231 --> 00:01:06,232
True.

14
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:07,692
Thanks, then!

15
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:08,818
‎Thank you.

16
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:11,738
Um, Hayami,

17
00:01:11,821 --> 00:01:13,698
you said before, right,

18
00:01:13,782 --> 00:01:16,451
that you came to Gate 24

19
00:01:17,202 --> 00:01:20,413
because you can't create rules
without knowing the field.

20
00:01:21,706 --> 00:01:22,582
Yes.

21
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:29,631
Honestly, when I get
absorbed in something,

22
00:01:29,714 --> 00:01:32,550
I sometimes forget the rules.

23
00:01:32,634 --> 00:01:34,928
Yes, I kind of noticed that.

24
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:43,353
But Hayami, you were on the side
that makes those rules.

25
00:01:46,272 --> 00:01:49,234
That's really amazing. I respect you.

26
00:01:54,322 --> 00:01:56,491
Just because a system is right

27
00:01:56,574 --> 00:01:59,911
doesn't mean the people
who make it are right.

28
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:06,167
-Passengers are here.
-Ah, okay!

29
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:17,846
<i>‎Announcement for all passengers.</i>

30
00:02:17,929 --> 00:02:23,268
<i>‎Flight 7H801 from Unitia</i>
<i>‎will be arriving soon.</i>

31
00:02:24,102 --> 00:02:28,690
<i>‎Please wait in the arrivals lounge.</i>

32
00:02:57,176 --> 00:02:59,846
-Endo, check it, please.
-Okay!

33
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:00,889
‎NOZOMI ENDO - QUARANTINE OFFICER

34
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:02,015
Excuse me.

35
00:03:02,098 --> 00:03:02,974
‎JUNKO TAMAI - CUSTOMS OFFICER

36
00:03:10,815 --> 00:03:13,192
MACHI MORI - CUSTOMS, MINISTRY OF FINANCE

37
00:03:31,711 --> 00:03:34,589
Um, Hayami, this person…

38
00:03:40,511 --> 00:03:42,764
Wait. This might be a quarantine issue.

39
00:03:42,847 --> 00:03:44,891
Who touches him changes who's responsible.

40
00:03:44,974 --> 00:03:46,684
This too.

41
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:48,811
But…

42
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:51,397
-I'm concerned.
-Wait…

43
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:56,903
Wait!

44
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:01,908
‎What?

45
00:04:05,495 --> 00:04:07,121
‎Please, everyone!

46
00:04:07,205 --> 00:04:09,165
-Huh? What?
-Huh?

47
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:12,919
Oh my…

48
00:04:13,002 --> 00:04:14,212
"Oh my" doesn't cut it!

49
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:24,138
That was a Murcia rabbit.

50
00:04:24,222 --> 00:04:25,765
-A Murcia rabbit?
-Yes.

51
00:04:25,848 --> 00:04:29,811
Distinct short round ears,
grayish-brown coat.

52
00:04:30,561 --> 00:04:31,646
I saw it with my own eyes.

53
00:04:31,729 --> 00:04:34,899
Don't just see it, catch it!

54
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:38,778
We closed the entrance.

55
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:40,280
RAN FUKASAWA - CHIEF HEARING OFFICER

56
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:43,032
We can't let an uninspected animal escape.

57
00:04:43,116 --> 00:04:45,034
Let's guide the passengers
to the main terminal.

58
00:04:45,118 --> 00:04:46,119
Yes, sir!

59
00:04:58,965 --> 00:05:00,508
What is this…

60
00:05:08,099 --> 00:05:09,600
Hey, you.

61
00:05:10,226 --> 00:05:12,937
-Go ahead, I'll guide you.
-No.

62
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:15,231
The inspection booth is right there.

63
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:17,567
-Let us through.
-It's currently closed.

64
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:20,069
-Please head toward the main terminal--
-It's far away.

65
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:23,614
Yes, it is. We apologize
for the inconvenience…

66
00:05:23,698 --> 00:05:26,326
Wait, wait, wait…

67
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:29,537
-Wait a second!
-What?

68
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:32,540
-You haven't cleared immigration yet.
-Then make it fast.

69
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:34,542
Like I said, um…

70
00:05:34,625 --> 00:05:36,669
-We're in a rush.
-Okay.

71
00:05:36,753 --> 00:05:38,963
Hayami, what should we do about that?

72
00:05:40,715 --> 00:05:42,967
You're always like that.

73
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:44,635
When something happens,
it's "not your call".

74
00:05:44,719 --> 00:05:45,762
Isn't that irresponsible?

75
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:49,265
Making arbitrary decisions
would be far more irresponsible.

76
00:05:51,642 --> 00:05:52,852
Go ahead and inspect them.

77
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:56,355
We'll sanitize this area,
so use the secondary room.

78
00:05:57,940 --> 00:06:00,526
-So? Did you find it?
-We can't find it anywhere!

79
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:01,694
Check every gap!

80
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:02,987
-Use gloves when you touch it.
-Okay!

81
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:04,822
May I see your passports?

82
00:06:06,324 --> 00:06:09,827
-May I check your luggage as well?
-Go ahead.

83
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:10,745
Thank you.

84
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:25,468
-Is this your child's luggage?
-Yes.

85
00:06:25,551 --> 00:06:27,929
He packed it himself,

86
00:06:28,012 --> 00:06:29,972
so I don't know what's in there.

87
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:37,313
Fumika Shinomiya

88
00:06:37,396 --> 00:06:41,025
-and Luis Anglard, right?
-Yes.

89
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:44,654
Pardon me for asking,
but does that mean you're not his mother?

90
00:06:45,321 --> 00:06:48,866
I'm his aunt. His mother's younger sister.

91
00:06:49,575 --> 00:06:50,618
Where are his parents?

92
00:06:52,495 --> 00:06:53,371
That's…

93
00:06:55,039 --> 00:06:58,501
-Excuse us. Come in.
-Hello. Pardon us.

94
00:06:58,584 --> 00:06:59,919
This is…

95
00:07:00,002 --> 00:07:02,338
This is Kijima
from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs--

96
00:07:02,421 --> 00:07:03,506
Oh, Hayami!

97
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:05,883
Long time no see.

98
00:07:06,759 --> 00:07:07,718
We haven't met since college.

99
00:07:07,802 --> 00:07:10,096
-Kijima…
-We'll talk later.

100
00:07:10,179 --> 00:07:11,097
‎MINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS
‎HIDETO KIJIMA

101
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:13,766
-You are Luis Anglard, correct?
-Yes, so?

102
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:17,228
I'm Kijima from the Consular Affairs
Bureau of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

103
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:21,441
Just now, we received
a call from Luis' father.

104
00:07:22,525 --> 00:07:25,194
He said, "My son has been kidnapped."

105
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:26,404
Kidnapped?

106
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:29,532
What are you talking about?

107
00:07:29,615 --> 00:07:31,200
Luis, you're safe now.

108
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:33,119
-Don't come near him!
-Oh, no, no.

109
00:07:33,202 --> 00:07:36,622
-Uh, we're just securing him.
-Please calm down.

110
00:07:36,706 --> 00:07:37,874
Now, Luis.

111
00:07:37,957 --> 00:07:40,001
Let's go back to your father.

112
00:07:50,344 --> 00:07:51,471
Oh my.

113
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:05,151
-Found it?
-No.

114
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:07,028
-Let's go that way.
-Okay!

115
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:12,033
-Let's split up.
-Okay.

116
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:13,826
-This way!
-Oh, there!

117
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:17,997
Where did it go?

118
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,999
MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE
FORESTRY AND FISHERIES

119
00:08:20,958 --> 00:08:22,752
Thank you, then.

120
00:08:22,835 --> 00:08:27,089
We are deeply sorry
for the inconvenience caused.

121
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:30,718
‎COUNSELOR OF BORDER CONTROL REFORM
‎MIDORI SUGIHARA

122
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:33,679
Well, well, Counselor Sugihara.

123
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:35,473
Airport Director.

124
00:08:36,807 --> 00:08:38,184
Are you here for that matter too?

125
00:08:38,267 --> 00:08:39,101
TAKAHIRO IKEURA
DIRECTOR OF KANTO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

126
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:41,979
Our staff is in chaos right now,

127
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:43,814
all because of a single rabbit.

128
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:46,192
I am so sorry for the trouble.

129
00:08:46,275 --> 00:08:50,613
If I recall, Gate 24 was a team
that crossed agency boundaries.

130
00:08:51,989 --> 00:08:55,159
Yet, for a quarantine matter,

131
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:57,328
you bowed down
to the Ministry of Agriculture

132
00:08:57,411 --> 00:09:00,706
and placed a burden on us
and the Ministry of Transport.

133
00:09:01,666 --> 00:09:04,919
What a splendid cross-agency team.

134
00:09:05,711 --> 00:09:07,672
As the person in charge of that team,

135
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:10,091
for now, I just want to resolve
the problem.

136
00:09:10,174 --> 00:09:11,133
You can give us your feedback later.

137
00:09:13,094 --> 00:09:14,387
That reminds me.

138
00:09:14,971 --> 00:09:19,600
It seems the Ministry of Foreign Affairs
is also involved with Gate 24 now.

139
00:09:20,393 --> 00:09:21,394
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs?

140
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:28,234
<i>Mommy, play with me.</i>

141
00:09:28,317 --> 00:09:31,654
M-my name is not Mommy.

142
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:36,200
It's Machi. Machi Mori.

143
00:09:39,036 --> 00:09:41,622
<i>Mommy, play with me.</i>

144
00:09:50,047 --> 00:09:52,466
His father is Julian Anglard.

145
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:55,094
A high-ranking government official
of the United Federation.

146
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:58,723
His mother is Japanese, Saeko Shinomiya.

147
00:09:58,806 --> 00:10:00,182
Apparently a picture book author.

148
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:03,311
They divorced about two weeks ago.

149
00:10:03,394 --> 00:10:05,354
Julian got custody.

150
00:10:06,188 --> 00:10:09,567
Saeko returned to Japan after that.

151
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:13,070
And that's Saeko's younger sister.

152
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:17,950
I told you, I just brought him
because my sister asked me to.

153
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:21,203
How is taking a child
to his mother kidnapping?

154
00:10:21,287 --> 00:10:23,039
-You know--
-Don't touch me!

155
00:10:23,122 --> 00:10:23,998
Ah, I'm sorry.

156
00:10:24,081 --> 00:10:24,915
‎INTERNATIONAL CRIMES DETECTIVE
‎IUCHI TAKAYA

157
00:10:24,999 --> 00:10:28,044
But you didn't get
the father's consent, right?

158
00:10:28,127 --> 00:10:30,963
In fact, the father reported it
to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs

159
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:32,923
as a missing person case.

160
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:35,384
Missing person.

161
00:10:36,135 --> 00:10:39,305
-That absolute piece of garbage!
-No, calm down… Ah, sorry!

162
00:10:41,057 --> 00:10:43,809
Where is Luis' mother?

163
00:11:04,705 --> 00:11:07,667
<i>Read me a picture book, Mommy.</i>

164
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:10,961
A picture book?

165
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:16,967
<i>Where is Daddy?</i>

166
00:11:17,051 --> 00:11:18,886
Daddy is…

167
00:11:21,972 --> 00:11:23,182
Matsuyama.

168
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:26,769
I heard about the case.
Leave the kid to me.

169
00:11:42,201 --> 00:11:43,202
What?

170
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:53,129
I thought I was the type kids liked.

171
00:11:56,257 --> 00:12:01,095
Maybe Luis doesn't get along
with adult men.

172
00:12:01,178 --> 00:12:05,307
But he hugged Hayami, right,
and called him "Daddy".

173
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:08,519
-I just happened to be where he ran.
-Thank you.

174
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:11,814
There's no point in looking for meaning
in everything a child says.

175
00:12:14,358 --> 00:12:18,070
Maybe he doesn't understand
the situation yet.

176
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:19,530
I think so too.

177
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:24,118
I mean, the mother is waiting
in the arrival lobby right now, right?

178
00:12:24,201 --> 00:12:25,494
Why not just let them meet?

179
00:12:25,578 --> 00:12:28,122
-No, that's--
-Of course, we can't do that.

180
00:12:28,205 --> 00:12:29,373
Do you know the Hague Convention?

181
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:32,626
The Hague Convention… That's, uh…

182
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:35,588
Children taken unlawfully across
international borders

183
00:12:35,671 --> 00:12:37,756
are, in principle, returned
to their original country.

184
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:39,592
That's the international agreement.

185
00:12:39,675 --> 00:12:42,553
If we let him meet the mother here,

186
00:12:42,636 --> 00:12:45,598
it could be seen as Japan
aiding in a child abduction.

187
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:48,517
-It'll become an international issue.
-I know,

188
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:50,478
but a mother and child
not being able to meet--

189
00:12:50,561 --> 00:12:52,521
This isn't a matter to judge
based on emotion.

190
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:55,107
I'm relieved, Hayami.

191
00:12:55,816 --> 00:12:57,109
Even after coming to a place like this,

192
00:12:57,193 --> 00:13:00,529
-you're still you.
-A place like this?

193
00:13:02,406 --> 00:13:03,991
What do you mean by that?

194
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:06,660
A video message,

195
00:13:07,411 --> 00:13:08,913
from Luis' father.

196
00:13:31,727 --> 00:13:33,103
<i>Bring Luis to me, now!</i>

197
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:34,647
I'm very sorry.

198
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:36,315
Hey there!

199
00:13:36,398 --> 00:13:38,192
-Please calm down.
-What?

200
00:13:38,275 --> 00:13:39,777
I'm with the police.

201
00:13:42,029 --> 00:13:43,614
You are Saeko Shinomiya, correct?

202
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:45,491
Do you have a moment?

203
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:48,244
-Ah, wait!
-Ma'am!

204
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:49,161
Out of my way!

205
00:13:49,245 --> 00:13:50,913
-You can't enter from here.
-Luis!

206
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:53,332
-Ms. Shinomiya, please calm down!
-Let go of me!

207
00:13:53,415 --> 00:13:54,542
-Luis!
-Please step back!

208
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:55,459
Don't touch me!

209
00:13:55,543 --> 00:13:58,003
Okay. Understood.

210
00:13:58,837 --> 00:14:00,673
-I'll go check on them.
-Thank you.

211
00:14:17,898 --> 00:14:18,941
Luis!

212
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:20,442
-Sorry, sorry!
-Luis!

213
00:14:20,526 --> 00:14:21,902
-Wait!
-Luis!

214
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:23,153
Move!

215
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:26,198
-Luis!
-Wait!

216
00:14:26,907 --> 00:14:28,784
Luis! Luis?

217
00:14:28,868 --> 00:14:31,579
Where are you? Luis!

218
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:35,207
You bastard… Hey!

219
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:37,126
You cowardly piece of trash!

220
00:14:37,209 --> 00:14:39,003
How dare you lie about a kidnapping!

221
00:14:39,795 --> 00:14:41,755
Stop messing with us!

222
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:43,257
Stop!

223
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:45,134
-Let go of me!
-Ms. Shinomiya, calm down.

224
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:47,386
If you make any more of a fuss,

225
00:14:47,469 --> 00:14:49,221
we will treat this as a diplomatic matter.

226
00:14:50,931 --> 00:14:51,765
If that happens,

227
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:54,101
your older sister
will be in an even worse situation.

228
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:55,603
Kijima…

229
00:14:55,686 --> 00:14:57,229
-Take her away.
-Okay.

230
00:14:57,313 --> 00:14:59,732
Make sure she never gets near Luis again.

231
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:02,192
Let go of me! Luis!

232
00:15:02,276 --> 00:15:03,903
Luis!

233
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:06,864
Isn't that going a bit too far?

234
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:08,657
It sounded like you were threatening her.

235
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:10,451
I know the Hague Convention exists,

236
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:12,828
but the final decision
on returning a child

237
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:15,497
isn't made by the Ministry
of Foreign Affairs, but by the court.

238
00:15:16,123 --> 00:15:18,167
The Ministry can only mediate
with the father,

239
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:20,210
it cannot take legal action.

240
00:15:20,294 --> 00:15:21,754
Custody of Luis belongs to the father.

241
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:25,716
What's wrong
with aligning with the father's wishes?

242
00:15:25,799 --> 00:15:28,928
We are dealing with a high-ranking
official of the United Federation.

243
00:15:29,511 --> 00:15:31,388
If this turns into an international issue,

244
00:15:32,056 --> 00:15:33,349
can you take responsibility?

245
00:15:38,812 --> 00:15:42,399
Know your place, Hayami.

246
00:15:45,069 --> 00:15:46,862
Know your place.

247
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:54,119
Mori, how's Luis doing?

248
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:55,913
Luis is…

249
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:00,542
‎Huh?

250
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:04,797
‎What?

251
00:16:11,136 --> 00:16:12,638
Where is Luis?

252
00:16:22,147 --> 00:16:23,065
Huh?

253
00:16:25,567 --> 00:16:27,111
Don't "huh" me!

254
00:16:30,114 --> 00:16:31,865
Yes, hello?

255
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:34,535
Did you find the rabbit?

256
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:38,080
What? A child?

257
00:16:48,257 --> 00:16:51,010
-Found him?
-Not yet.

258
00:16:52,469 --> 00:16:53,804
Um…

259
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:56,849
This is a piece of a keychain.

260
00:16:56,932 --> 00:16:58,559
-A keychain?
-Yes.

261
00:16:59,977 --> 00:17:02,021
It was on Luis' tablet.

262
00:17:06,233 --> 00:17:07,192
I saw it, for sure.

263
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:45,522
Hello.

264
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:47,566
Are you playing hide-and-seek?

265
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:55,407
So you're saying you lost track

266
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:57,367
of both a quarantined animal and a child

267
00:17:57,451 --> 00:18:00,329
who is involved in an international case
at the same time.

268
00:18:01,121 --> 00:18:02,456
-Yes.
-Yes.

269
00:18:03,624 --> 00:18:04,833
I'm sorry.

270
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:09,546
This will add another item to the manual.

271
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:10,964
Nothing but manuals…

272
00:18:12,716 --> 00:18:15,969
At any rate, I'm glad the boy is safe.

273
00:18:16,637 --> 00:18:19,640
As for the search for the rabbit,
let's reorganize our approach.

274
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:21,558
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

275
00:18:22,392 --> 00:18:24,269
About Luis,

276
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:27,981
it was decided that our department
will look after him until the next flight.

277
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:31,026
Make sure not to take
your eyes off him this time.

278
00:18:31,944 --> 00:18:32,778
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes.

279
00:18:34,279 --> 00:18:35,489
Everyone, got a minute?

280
00:18:38,951 --> 00:18:42,246
Then Hayami and Mori,
do your best to watch the kid.

281
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:46,834
-What?
-I mean, you're Daddy and Mommy, right?

282
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:21,618
Um…

283
00:19:22,202 --> 00:19:24,788
Hayami, look.

284
00:19:27,332 --> 00:19:29,918
A straw hat, a bug net…

285
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:33,380
A ring float…

286
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:39,469
According to what was said earlier,
Luis packed this himself.

287
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:43,265
It looks like luggage
for going on a picnic…

288
00:19:44,725 --> 00:19:47,978
Maybe he intended
to play together with his mother.

289
00:19:51,607 --> 00:19:53,442
That's just speculation.

290
00:19:54,776 --> 00:19:57,529
Yes, it's speculation.

291
00:19:58,739 --> 00:19:59,656
But

292
00:20:00,282 --> 00:20:01,617
the items are saying so.

293
00:20:04,536 --> 00:20:10,083
Did he try to run away earlier
because he wanted to see his mom?

294
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:30,062
<i>Read me a picture book.</i>

295
00:20:31,563 --> 00:20:34,483
-A picture book?
-He mentioned it earlier too,

296
00:20:34,566 --> 00:20:37,152
so I prepared a few books.

297
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:51,625
It's picture book data.

298
00:20:53,877 --> 00:20:56,922
So that's what it was about.

299
00:20:58,048 --> 00:21:00,008
Saeko Shinomiya.

300
00:21:00,592 --> 00:21:02,636
Did his mother make these books?

301
00:21:05,138 --> 00:21:08,433
What is this?

302
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:30,289
-<i>to you.</i>
-Reading aloud for her child…

303
00:21:35,043 --> 00:21:38,839
Saeko probably recorded this video
thinking she might get

304
00:21:38,922 --> 00:21:40,757
separated from Luis.

305
00:21:42,634 --> 00:21:46,388
Luis looks happy to see his mother too.

306
00:21:48,849 --> 00:21:50,058
Can this

307
00:21:50,892 --> 00:21:53,478
really be called a kidnapping?

308
00:21:54,021 --> 00:21:58,567
From the luggage, it certainly
looks like he came to see his mother.

309
00:21:58,650 --> 00:21:59,484
Yes.

310
00:21:59,568 --> 00:22:04,364
That video is also full
of a mother's love.

311
00:22:05,324 --> 00:22:06,825
Love, is it?

312
00:22:07,451 --> 00:22:10,078
But a mother's love

313
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:12,789
and whether abduction is legal
are two different matters.

314
00:22:12,873 --> 00:22:14,416
Well, yes.

315
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:18,920
I'm also concerned about the father.

316
00:22:19,004 --> 00:22:20,213
The father?

317
00:22:20,297 --> 00:22:21,923
He never once uttered

318
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:24,551
his son's name, nor did he try to see him.

319
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:27,554
I have a child too,

320
00:22:28,930 --> 00:22:30,932
but if I found out they were safe,

321
00:22:31,016 --> 00:22:33,435
the first thing
I'd want is to see their face.

322
00:22:34,019 --> 00:22:35,979
I was bothered by that too.

323
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:41,443
Plus, Julian used the phrasing
of "controlling" his own child.

324
00:22:44,863 --> 00:22:45,822
Control?

325
00:22:46,323 --> 00:22:49,618
<i>Mommy, please read me a picture book.</i>

326
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:51,036
M-me?

327
00:22:54,456 --> 00:22:57,167
<i>Super Daddy.</i>

328
00:23:07,302 --> 00:23:08,678
Excuse me.

329
00:23:09,846 --> 00:23:10,931
-Hello.
-Hey, there.

330
00:23:11,014 --> 00:23:12,557
Hello, Counselor.

331
00:23:12,641 --> 00:23:14,309
How is the interrogation going?

332
00:23:15,268 --> 00:23:16,561
We're struggling.

333
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:20,565
However, I feel like we can't definitively
say it's just a kidnapping.

334
00:23:21,191 --> 00:23:22,275
What do you mean?

335
00:23:22,984 --> 00:23:26,613
When we restrained
the mother earlier, I saw it.

336
00:23:30,450 --> 00:23:33,495
<i>Bruises on her arm and neck.</i>

337
00:23:33,995 --> 00:23:35,080
Bruises?

338
00:23:35,163 --> 00:23:38,041
They're most likely…

339
00:23:43,421 --> 00:23:44,422
That's right.

340
00:23:45,048 --> 00:23:47,592
Julian has always used violence
against my older sister.

341
00:23:47,676 --> 00:23:50,887
Why didn't you say so at first?

342
00:23:52,097 --> 00:23:53,849
If I said it, would you have believed it?

343
00:23:55,684 --> 00:23:57,978
When talk of divorce came up,

344
00:23:58,937 --> 00:24:00,814
my sister formally reported it.

345
00:24:02,023 --> 00:24:04,609
To her lawyer, to the consulate.

346
00:24:05,318 --> 00:24:07,404
She even had people testify for her.

347
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:10,115
And yet,

348
00:24:11,491 --> 00:24:15,495
before we knew it, everything was erased.

349
00:24:16,705 --> 00:24:19,958
Julian crushed it all.

350
00:24:22,043 --> 00:24:23,086
So now,

351
00:24:24,337 --> 00:24:28,258
this is the only way
for my sister to see Luis.

352
00:24:31,428 --> 00:24:33,138
I feel bad for the mom.

353
00:24:33,805 --> 00:24:38,351
As for me, I always end up
thinking that a child

354
00:24:38,435 --> 00:24:40,395
should be allowed
to stay with their mother.

355
00:24:40,478 --> 00:24:41,605
That's true.

356
00:24:41,688 --> 00:24:43,273
Even so, there's the Hague Convention.

357
00:24:43,857 --> 00:24:47,152
It feels frustrating when mother
and child are right over there.

358
00:24:49,613 --> 00:24:51,323
Huh? Wait a second.

359
00:24:52,157 --> 00:24:53,033
This is…

360
00:24:53,867 --> 00:24:55,118
Seika!

361
00:24:55,744 --> 00:24:56,828
Look.

362
00:24:58,914 --> 00:25:01,166
WARNING: FLAMMABLE

363
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:03,543
It's a rabbit bite mark.

364
00:25:03,627 --> 00:25:05,003
It's still fresh.

365
00:25:05,629 --> 00:25:07,380
Does that mean it's nearby?!

366
00:25:07,464 --> 00:25:09,758
ALCOHOL HAND SANITIZER

367
00:25:10,342 --> 00:25:11,468
Kijima.

368
00:25:12,719 --> 00:25:14,262
Did you know?

369
00:25:14,346 --> 00:25:16,806
Julian was using violence
against his ex-wife.

370
00:25:19,059 --> 00:25:21,436
It's just the ex-wife's claim, right?

371
00:25:22,062 --> 00:25:25,565
-There's no evidence.
-It's possible Julian erased the evidence.

372
00:25:29,653 --> 00:25:31,738
Are you intending to treat
a United Federation

373
00:25:31,821 --> 00:25:34,783
high official as a domestic abuser
based on mere possibility?

374
00:25:36,493 --> 00:25:40,455
If such groundless rumors were to spread,
it would affect Julian's honor.

375
00:25:41,122 --> 00:25:44,417
Furthermore, it affects the credibility
of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

376
00:25:49,965 --> 00:25:52,425
So that's why you rushed things so much.

377
00:25:55,262 --> 00:25:57,222
This is for the country.

378
00:25:57,305 --> 00:25:59,766
You of all people should understand
what's important

379
00:26:00,308 --> 00:26:01,476
for the organization.

380
00:26:02,769 --> 00:26:03,770
No.

381
00:26:04,562 --> 00:26:07,399
It's because you didn't understand that

382
00:26:08,566 --> 00:26:12,612
that you were transferred
to a place like this, right?

383
00:26:32,132 --> 00:26:33,216
I'm sorry.

384
00:26:33,883 --> 00:26:36,720
Luis said he needed to go to the bathroom.

385
00:26:41,141 --> 00:26:42,475
<i>Hayami, huh?</i>

386
00:26:42,559 --> 00:26:46,062
I'm bothered by the fact
that Hayami isn't saying anything.

387
00:26:46,146 --> 00:26:49,024
He has had it rough.

388
00:26:49,774 --> 00:26:52,527
When Hayami was
at the Ministry of Justice,

389
00:26:52,610 --> 00:26:55,280
he was burning with a sense of duty.

390
00:26:55,363 --> 00:26:57,615
<i>He wanted to renovate the system,</i>

391
00:26:57,699 --> 00:27:00,243
<i>to save from unjust suffering.</i>

392
00:27:01,077 --> 00:27:04,873
<i>He especially focused on one case.</i>

393
00:27:05,373 --> 00:27:06,499
<i>At a certain company,</i>

394
00:27:06,583 --> 00:27:08,877
<i>a young female employee suffered</i>

395
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:11,546
<i>from long working hours</i>
<i>and pressure from her superior</i>

396
00:27:11,629 --> 00:27:14,674
<i>and took her own life.</i>

397
00:27:14,758 --> 00:27:17,010
The company covered up
the records entirely.

398
00:27:17,093 --> 00:27:20,138
-Calm down, Hayami.
-We should investigate thoroughly.

399
00:27:24,100 --> 00:27:25,393
This company

400
00:27:25,935 --> 00:27:28,855
has many of our alumni working in it.

401
00:27:34,527 --> 00:27:38,365
A person involved with the law
was overlooking illegal activity.

402
00:27:38,448 --> 00:27:40,200
It's ironic.

403
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:44,788
And so, what did Hayami do?

404
00:27:44,871 --> 00:27:46,206
Good morning.

405
00:27:46,289 --> 00:27:49,918
<i>After agonizing, it seems</i>
<i>he tried to blow the whistle.</i>

406
00:27:52,170 --> 00:27:53,463
<i>However…</i>

407
00:27:58,218 --> 00:28:01,179
NOTICE OF TRANSFER

408
00:28:14,401 --> 00:28:15,610
I told you, Hayami.

409
00:28:17,404 --> 00:28:19,406
Know your place.

410
00:28:53,690 --> 00:28:54,858
-I…
-Hayami…

411
00:29:01,030 --> 00:29:02,949
I made a mistake.

412
00:29:06,077 --> 00:29:08,455
I made a mistake at a crucial moment.

413
00:29:11,291 --> 00:29:12,709
As a result, I'm here.

414
00:29:14,669 --> 00:29:17,630
<i>Daddy, please read me a picture book.</i>

415
00:29:19,132 --> 00:29:20,759
I told you, I'm not your daddy.

416
00:29:30,518 --> 00:29:33,313
Um, you're mistaken, Hayami.

417
00:29:33,855 --> 00:29:34,981
I figured it out.

418
00:29:39,694 --> 00:29:41,571
Look at this picture book.

419
00:29:42,113 --> 00:29:43,490
<i>Super Daddy.</i>

420
00:29:44,157 --> 00:29:48,286
It's a story about
an ordinary father who becomes

421
00:29:48,369 --> 00:29:50,789
a superhero to protect his child.

422
00:29:51,706 --> 00:29:54,083
Doesn't this Super Daddy
look like you, Hayami?

423
00:29:55,043 --> 00:29:56,002
Me?

424
00:29:57,253 --> 00:29:58,254
He looks just like you.

425
00:30:01,382 --> 00:30:02,258
Actually…

426
00:30:04,302 --> 00:30:06,930
this "mommy" here looks like you.

427
00:30:07,680 --> 00:30:09,474
-Me?
-Somewhat.

428
00:30:13,436 --> 00:30:14,270
I see.

429
00:30:16,022 --> 00:30:17,690
So that's why you called us…

430
00:30:19,234 --> 00:30:20,860
Daddy and Mommy.

431
00:30:21,528 --> 00:30:25,657
To Luis, Hayami, you are a superhero.

432
00:30:26,199 --> 00:30:29,494
This story seems to be
Luis' absolute favorite.

433
00:30:30,119 --> 00:30:34,958
But this is the only one
with no video of his mother reading it.

434
00:30:35,041 --> 00:30:35,917
True.

435
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:39,420
That's why he wanted us
to read it instead.

436
00:30:39,504 --> 00:30:41,339
The mystery is solved.

437
00:30:42,423 --> 00:30:43,424
Hayami,

438
00:30:44,968 --> 00:30:46,010
will you read it for him?

439
00:30:47,387 --> 00:30:51,057
-Me?
-You're his hero. Yes.

440
00:30:58,731 --> 00:31:00,358
Mori, you read it.

441
00:31:01,317 --> 00:31:03,194
I don't deserve to be called a hero.

442
00:31:03,278 --> 00:31:05,989
There's nothing I can do.
I'll leave you to it.

443
00:31:18,293 --> 00:31:19,294
All right.

444
00:31:24,549 --> 00:31:28,595
<i>Rabbits have a habit of hiding</i>
<i>in narrow, dark places.</i>

445
00:31:28,678 --> 00:31:29,596
Ready.

446
00:31:30,305 --> 00:31:35,143
<i>We will play audio of a mother rabbit</i>
<i>to draw it out.</i>

447
00:31:40,398 --> 00:31:41,816
All ready here.

448
00:31:43,776 --> 00:31:46,195
I hope it goes well.

449
00:31:46,279 --> 00:31:48,823
<i>I want to catch the rabbit too.</i>

450
00:31:51,242 --> 00:31:52,577
You too, Luis?

451
00:31:54,746 --> 00:31:57,957
<i>I want to let the rabbit go home.</i>

452
00:32:00,251 --> 00:32:04,380
-Hayami, then should we also--
-Of course not.

453
00:32:04,464 --> 00:32:06,382
More importantly,
it's almost time for the flight.

454
00:32:06,466 --> 00:32:07,508
We have to prepare.

455
00:32:11,846 --> 00:32:14,349
-I told you no.
-Um…

456
00:32:16,809 --> 00:32:18,895
This sound… It's not me.

457
00:32:51,052 --> 00:32:51,928
Hayami.

458
00:32:59,185 --> 00:33:01,562
It's okay, Daddy will catch it for us.

459
00:33:01,646 --> 00:33:02,981
I told you, I'm not Daddy.

460
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:08,444
All right…

461
00:33:36,848 --> 00:33:38,266
Hayami…

462
00:33:44,731 --> 00:33:47,233
‎KANTO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT TERMINAL 2

463
00:33:47,316 --> 00:33:50,611
We finished sanitizing everything,
so it's fine now.

464
00:33:50,695 --> 00:33:51,863
Thank you very much.

465
00:33:51,946 --> 00:33:54,032
It seems that the rabbit was stolen

466
00:33:54,115 --> 00:33:56,284
from a protection
and breeding facility in Unitia.

467
00:33:56,367 --> 00:33:59,037
After inspection, it will be returned
to the original facility.

468
00:33:59,954 --> 00:34:01,080
Thank goodness.

469
00:34:19,599 --> 00:34:21,059
<i>I don't want to go home.</i>

470
00:34:24,270 --> 00:34:27,148
<i>Papa was being mean to Mama.</i>

471
00:34:28,691 --> 00:34:31,944
<i>I don't want to see Papa.</i>
<i>I want to see Mama.</i>

472
00:34:34,906 --> 00:34:35,907
Hayami.

473
00:34:36,407 --> 00:34:38,910
Can't we do something?

474
00:34:39,535 --> 00:34:43,831
I don't think Luis
could say this to anyone.

475
00:34:43,915 --> 00:34:47,752
But he thinks you could help him.

476
00:34:48,419 --> 00:34:50,671
To Luis, you're a--

477
00:34:56,177 --> 00:34:57,887
Making these decisions
isn't part of my job.

478
00:35:00,306 --> 00:35:01,682
Sorry to keep you waiting, Luis.

479
00:35:03,810 --> 00:35:05,478
Hayami, thanks for taking care of him.

480
00:35:05,561 --> 00:35:07,480
Looks like we'll make the flight in time.

481
00:35:10,942 --> 00:35:12,902
U-um…

482
00:35:13,986 --> 00:35:16,989
Could you wait just a little longer?

483
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:22,495
Luis seems to want to stay here…

484
00:35:23,079 --> 00:35:26,207
<i>Daddy, please read me a picture book.</i>

485
00:35:27,208 --> 00:35:28,668
There's no time for that.

486
00:35:29,168 --> 00:35:30,962
Um…

487
00:35:33,756 --> 00:35:34,674
That's right, Hayami.

488
00:35:35,424 --> 00:35:36,509
That's good.

489
00:35:39,679 --> 00:35:42,807
<i>I told you, Hayami. Know your place.</i>

490
00:35:51,149 --> 00:35:52,608
Can't be helped.

491
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:55,171
Wait, Kijima.

492
00:37:01,302 --> 00:37:02,595
I told you.

493
00:37:03,137 --> 00:37:05,181
The final authority on whether
to return a child

494
00:37:05,264 --> 00:37:07,767
is the court,
not the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

495
00:37:09,477 --> 00:37:11,187
Judgments aside,

496
00:37:11,270 --> 00:37:12,688
a contact came from the father

497
00:37:12,772 --> 00:37:15,191
with custody treating it
as a missing person report.

498
00:37:15,858 --> 00:37:16,984
There's also the Hague Convention.

499
00:37:18,152 --> 00:37:19,237
And besides,

500
00:37:19,904 --> 00:37:21,572
this has nothing to do with Immigration.

501
00:37:34,627 --> 00:37:37,797
This is my workplace, and that boy
is a child I was in charge of.

502
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:39,840
I can't just say it has
nothing to do with me.

503
00:37:40,925 --> 00:37:43,010
This is my problem.

504
00:37:44,262 --> 00:37:45,096
Hayami…

505
00:38:14,083 --> 00:38:16,168
Hayami, you…

506
00:38:28,431 --> 00:38:30,349
Is this going to be okay?

507
00:38:30,433 --> 00:38:32,143
-He will be held accountable.
-No, not at all.

508
00:38:32,226 --> 00:38:34,937
Is this really going to become
an international issue?

509
00:38:35,021 --> 00:38:37,398
-Wait, Mori!
-Um, Hayami!

510
00:38:37,982 --> 00:38:40,568
Hayami, Hayami, Hayami.

511
00:38:44,822 --> 00:38:47,283
Look at this. It was in the trash can,

512
00:38:48,284 --> 00:38:50,578
the video of <i>Super Daddy</i>.

513
00:39:17,646 --> 00:39:18,731
Hayami!

514
00:39:19,273 --> 00:39:22,735
You apologize too.
You say careless things without any proof.

515
00:39:24,028 --> 00:39:26,822
If it's proof you want, we have it.

516
00:39:27,406 --> 00:39:28,407
What?

517
00:39:38,542 --> 00:39:40,795
This is a video of Saeko
reading a picture book to Luis.

518
00:39:50,471 --> 00:39:51,389
What is this?

519
00:40:04,026 --> 00:40:05,653
<i>Ba ba bam!</i>

520
00:41:42,124 --> 00:41:45,961
<i>So Julian withdrew</i>
<i>the missing person report, right?</i>

521
00:41:46,545 --> 00:41:50,633
Yes. Not only that, but he's also
handing over Luis' custody to Saeko.

522
00:41:51,634 --> 00:41:56,514
In the end, his own status
was more important than his child.

523
00:41:57,723 --> 00:41:59,266
But thank goodness.

524
00:41:59,934 --> 00:42:04,688
Being in a place where Luis
can feel safe is what matters most.

525
00:42:05,523 --> 00:42:06,815
That's very like you, Fukasawa.

526
00:42:07,525 --> 00:42:09,068
I'm a parent, after all.

527
00:42:10,402 --> 00:42:14,615
-Luis! Luis!
-Mama!

528
00:42:16,992 --> 00:42:18,869
That's overwhelming.

529
00:42:19,995 --> 00:42:21,247
Yes.

530
00:42:25,793 --> 00:42:27,670
Um, Hayami.

531
00:42:30,130 --> 00:42:32,800
You said earlier, right,

532
00:42:33,342 --> 00:42:36,178
that you came here
because you made a mistake.

533
00:42:39,890 --> 00:42:41,183
Is that really true?

534
00:42:46,772 --> 00:42:47,815
<i>Hayami.</i>

535
00:42:48,857 --> 00:42:49,775
Here.

536
00:42:51,569 --> 00:42:54,280
This plan has come up
from the Cabinet Secretariat.

537
00:42:54,905 --> 00:42:57,992
It's a plan made by a counselor
burning with ideals.

538
00:42:58,075 --> 00:43:00,911
Eliminating agency walls
to unite the field as one.

539
00:43:01,704 --> 00:43:04,873
Nobody takes it seriously.
It's a pipe dream.

540
00:43:09,253 --> 00:43:13,757
THE PLAN FOR GATE 24

541
00:43:13,841 --> 00:43:15,551
EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

542
00:43:20,639 --> 00:43:22,099
I wonder.

543
00:43:24,351 --> 00:43:25,311
What's wrong?

544
00:43:25,811 --> 00:43:26,812
No, nothing.

545
00:43:31,025 --> 00:43:35,446
Everyone, thank you
so much for everything.

546
00:43:36,447 --> 00:43:37,656
It's great, isn't it?

547
00:43:37,740 --> 00:43:41,160
This time, it was thanks to Hayami.

548
00:43:41,243 --> 00:43:42,494
Me?

549
00:43:43,454 --> 00:43:44,538
Because he's a hero.

550
00:43:49,543 --> 00:43:51,086
I'm not a hero at all.

551
00:43:52,504 --> 00:43:54,548
-You're not?
-No.

552
00:43:56,884 --> 00:44:00,262
I'm just an immigration officer.

553
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:04,224
Oh my…

554
00:44:10,731 --> 00:44:13,192
Hayami. Hayami.

555
00:44:17,029 --> 00:44:17,905
Come on!

556
00:44:44,515 --> 00:44:47,434
‎-The high five tour.
‎-What!?

557
00:44:47,518 --> 00:44:48,977
<i>‎A Korean idol group.</i>

558
00:44:49,061 --> 00:44:50,979
<i>‎They're world famous.</i>

559
00:44:51,063 --> 00:44:54,149
‎I can't allow you to enter the country
‎without a passport.

560
00:44:54,233 --> 00:44:55,109
‎Where did you work before this?

561
00:44:55,192 --> 00:44:56,652
‎Machi Mori?

562
00:44:56,735 --> 00:44:58,487
‎-It's Yuki.
‎-Ms. Yuki…

563
00:44:58,570 --> 00:44:59,863
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
